#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finger is a program to display information about users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If finger is enabled on the remote machine, you may be given information on "
"the user's real name, if they are currently logged in, if they have mail and "
"the text of their <filename>.plan</filename> file in their home folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finger is normally associated with a user@hostname address, which may or may "
"not be the same as a users email address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most Internet Service Providers no longer allow finger access, so, you may "
"find that you get no useful answer for most people."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other people use their local <filename>.plan</filename> file to hold such "
"information as <acronym>PGP</acronym> keys, the fact they are on vacation, "
"and all sorts of information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the finger kioslave like this: <userinput>finger://"
"<replaceable>username</replaceable>@<replaceable>hostname</replaceable></"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "See the manual: <ulink url=\"man:/finger\">finger</ulink>."
msgstr ""
